Z||000000||BAM-BAM||07-07-2000||11:40 PM||||  What is the real difference in the spings of an 84-87 vs. an 88? Are they really that different? Please let me know, a friend needs help! TIA!!!!!<P>  Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||07-07-2000||11:52 PM||||The 88 front springs are different lengths than the 84/87 (I think the diameter may be different too.) As for the back I think they are the same but am not sure. One of these days I am going to find someone with an 88 that has the tires off so I can see exactly what differences there are.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||07-08-2000||12:13 AM||||  Oreif, let's say that the length is the only consideration. I have read other post's of people who felt that the 88 had a bit of a front rake, making it appear that the front end was set higher than the rear. Therefore, they have cut the stock length of front springs to compensate. Now, with length being the only consideration, would they not be interchangable? Or, is there some sort of geometric considerations that would preclude this type of swap? This is an interesting question, one that some  of our more esteemed an highly experienced Fiero'ns might be able to answer. There is still time, so I am sure that answers to my querry will be forthcoming. Thanks Oreif, for your input. <P>  Late, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 07-08-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000003||gixxer||07-08-2000||12:32 AM||||'88 WS6 front springs:<BR>12" free length<BR>~6.25 active coils<BR>3.875 coil diameter (about wire centerline)<BR>.5" wire diameter<BR>Both coil wire ends bent flat<BR>Spring rate ~236# per inch. Non WS6 is probably higher. <BR>A-arm ratio between spring travel and lower ball joint travel is .57 <BR>Have fun.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||07-08-2000||12:38 AM||||   Now we have half of the puzzle, anyone else?<P>  B-B<P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000005||theogre||07-08-2000||12:14 PM||||If you are looking for stiffer springs and sway cheap for a base coupe get a set from a GT or spourt coup. Those are stiffer than base. My SC will rattle your teeth compaired to a base set. I drive hard and still wouldn't want to get stiffer springs than these.||||reg||1
